From 7ce62c040d6d0ff7c6802ce8a7accecf662763a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:51:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(tools): document component table and undoable
 assembly commands

The document holds shared tool components (DocumentComponents) and
each tool its component stack (ToolAssembly). Four undoable commands:
UpsertDocumentComponent, EditDocumentComponent (live update of every
tool built from the component, in one undo step, refused whole by
name), DeleteDocumentComponent (refuses a used component, names the
tools) and SetToolAssembly (lands the derived ToolDef and ToolBody).
Operations go Stale by their stamps. DeleteTool keeps the stack.

Fixes #3644

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
